From 4eff2691da8cc027aed26c68aba09e9073881385 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:54:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): cards never park forever without showing as
 waiting on someone [daveey]

Root cause of 2026-10-21 "tasks not running, not blocked" (card t_96bf7912):

1. Respawn guard: a completion-gate refusal ("PR acceptance ...") is never
   blocker_auth. Any guard hold is capped (blocker_auth 30 min, others 6 h,
   shared_blocker exempt): past the cap the dispatcher blocks the card with
   the guard reason, since a held card never runs and the breaker can't trip.
2. PR acceptance: a closed-unmerged PR is classification closed_unmerged;
   the catch-all names the failed phase + exception type and no longer says
   "check gh authentication". A binding to a closed-unmerged PR may be
   replaced by a new published_pr in the same repo (pr_rebound event).
3. Scheduled invariant: every schedule_task park carries wake_at (marker or
   24 h default); a card awaiting a human answer can't be scheduled; the
   dispatcher wakes legacy wake-less parks at their implied time (reason
   marker, else park + 24 h) and moves human-kind ones to blocked. New
   diagnostic scheduled_without_wake.
4. Block-loop escalations in triage count as waiting on the user:
   diagnostics escalated_waiting_on_user + waiting_behind_user (todo child of
   a parent that needs the user); board_stats/`kanban stats` report
   waiting_on_user.
5. Top-level launches (serve/dashboard/gui/desktop/gateway, Electron main,
   and the post-update Desktop reopen via `open`) drop a leaked kanban
   worker / delegate-child identity env. A worker's `hermes update` reopened
   Hermes.app with HERMES_DELEGATED_CHILD_CONTEXT + HERMES_KANBAN_*, so
   every Desktop chat's kanban tools refused.
